      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You could leverage the legal concept of \"de minimis\" to argue that the encroachment is too trivial to warrant denying the entire rezoning application. Furthermore, you might invoke administrative discretion, suggesting that the spirit and intent of the zoning code—promoting desired land use—outweigh the technicality of a minor setback violation. Focus your presentation on how resolving this small issue enables a larger, beneficial community development.",
      "source": "target",
